  "design_principle": "Fixed MATCHED candidates: the same candidate_id maps to exactly the same theta across all damping levels and all repeat sessions (theta is NEVER redrawn from a session seed or the hidden state). grasp_offset_local_y is confined to the reliable-grasp zone [-0.02,0.02] (capability map: this band = 1.00 success) so grasp offset is NOT the failure driver and does NOT dominate the candidates; differentiation is along max_pos_step x pull_lead so the hidden damping can change which candidate is best. Archetypes span conservative -> aggressive. c4_aggressive (large step + large pull carrot) is expected to be fastest at low damping but most likely to detach/timeout at high damping; c0_conservative (small step + short carrot) is expected to be slower but most robust at high damping. grasp_offset values are jittered symmetrically and are deliberately NOT correlated with the aggressiveness ordering, so no single grasp offset explains the candidate ranking. These archetypes are frozen from capability-map / micro-sweep priors BEFORE any outcome is observed; they are not tuned to produce a result.",
